WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.010 --> 00:00:05.760
Like everything, humans are made up of atoms.

00:00:05.760 --> 00:00:11.410
But what’s interesting, is how we behave
so very similar to them.

00:00:11.410 --> 00:00:18.140
Atoms share electron pairs with other atoms
in order to become stable and form covalent

00:00:18.140 --> 00:00:19.910
bonds.

00:00:19.910 --> 00:00:25.960
Human relationships are just like that of
covalent bonds and reflect the same process

00:00:25.960 --> 00:00:29.350
of give-and-take.

00:00:29.350 --> 00:00:34.160
Relationships develop out of some divine-like
push and pull.

00:00:34.160 --> 00:00:41.010
When we allow it, we are magnetized towards
other people that are compatible with our

00:00:41.010 --> 00:00:42.010
polarity.

00:00:42.010 --> 00:00:48.440
Two people become into one mutual life when
a stable bond is formed.

00:00:48.440 --> 00:00:55.190
These bonds are formed all through life, attempting
to balance out all of our unstable forces

00:00:55.190 --> 00:00:57.710
in the process.

00:00:57.710 --> 00:01:04.530
In theory, this is a beautiful system that
guarantees balanced and receptive relationships

00:01:04.530 --> 00:01:06.610
throughout life.

00:01:06.610 --> 00:01:15.000
But then why does it seem like there are so
many challenges associated with human social-life?

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:20.930
Why is true friendship and partnership so
hard to find?

00:01:20.930 --> 00:01:25.630
This challenge rises out of our insecurities
and fears.

00:01:25.630 --> 00:01:31.340
Our fear of being our self and having others
dislike it.

00:01:31.340 --> 00:01:38.390
But when we submit to this fear and hide behind
its wall, we inadvertently prevent our electron

00:01:38.390 --> 00:01:42.420
pairs from being fully revealed to the world.

00:01:42.420 --> 00:01:50.090
Our whole self hides behind the wall and the
polarized system of push and pull becomes

00:01:50.090 --> 00:01:52.060
broken.

00:01:52.060 --> 00:01:56.880
It is like someone holding their hand in front
of a camera lens.

00:01:56.880 --> 00:01:59.170
No one can see the subject.

00:01:59.170 --> 00:02:02.460
No one can enjoy the subject.

00:02:02.460 --> 00:02:09.450
For successful social relationships to occur,
your whole image must be visible.

00:02:09.450 --> 00:02:16.010
By removing your hand from the lens, you reveal
your true self to the world and allow others

00:02:16.010 --> 00:02:18.520
to do the same.

00:02:18.520 --> 00:02:24.770
If you want people to truly care for you and
allow you to care for them, you must be willing

00:02:24.770 --> 00:02:28.549
to present your full self without fear.

00:02:28.549 --> 00:02:36.730
If, instead, you hide behind fear’s wall,
you will never find the stability and connection

00:02:36.730 --> 00:02:40.209
we all so desire in life.

00:02:40.209 --> 00:02:47.409
Instead of forming balance like atoms, you
will only form temporariness and insecurity.

00:02:47.409 --> 00:02:55.340
Like a cigarette, your life will be smoked
away by those you encounter in life.

00:02:55.340 --> 00:03:00.739
Your ashes will be flicked into the wind until
nothing remains.

00:03:00.739 --> 00:03:07.180
You will treat others the same way and feel
slight and temporary pleasure from your relationships,

00:03:07.180 --> 00:03:14.430
but the sensations will soon dissipate and
you will soon be left with nothing.

00:03:14.430 --> 00:03:18.750
Not everyone is going to match with your polarity
in life.

00:03:18.750 --> 00:03:24.139
Accept this and do not bother trying to force
relationships with those who do not.

00:03:24.139 --> 00:03:31.709
You must, instead, search only for those who
DO match with your truest self.

00:03:31.709 --> 00:03:37.371
Like when you are scanning the radio and come
across a station with poor reception, you

00:03:37.371 --> 00:03:42.940
must not stay and listen to the static of
meaningless social relationships.

00:03:42.940 --> 00:03:59.239
You must keep scanning until you find value
and clarity.

